A||||8||Fiero_24||What should I do about a dead beat bidder?||||5||
Z||000000||Fiero_24||11-27-2001||08:23 PM||||I had an item on ebay that ended Friday afternoon Nov-23-01 14:41:58 PST.  The buyer has not responded as of now (7:22PM 11/27/01).  What should I do?  I emailed them 3 times, and the one time I gave the 3 business days starting Monday 11/26/01 to pay up or at least contact me.  Any suggestions?  Here is a link to the auction:<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1299343490" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1299343490</A> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroMontreal||11-27-2001||08:37 PM||||File a "non-paying bidder alert" .. see if that does anything.. if not.. try to contact him again... give him a week or 2 at the most.. then go to re-list and leave him a - feedback..<P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif">   <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-27-2001||09:02 PM||||With all the Ebay stuff we sell, We send out an Email on the day it closes and we wait the 3 business days. If no reply we send out a 24 hour notice. If we do not hear from them within the 24 hour notice, we give negative feedback and re-list the item. You also have the option of asking the second highest bidder if they are still interested in the item at their last bid. The person who won your auction just opened their Ebay account that day. He also only bid on your auction.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroFanaticus2||11-27-2001||09:41 PM||||I always try to call the person on the telephone if they ignore emails, then I inform them about the legally binding contract they entered when bidding.  Most of the time it works, sometimes it doesn't.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||11-28-2001||06:12 AM||||I had one not respond for almost a week. Turned out he was away on vacation and away from his computer. He did apologize and sent the money rite away. If you want make a note of it to Ebay and relist it. I always make sure in description, I say how long after action I wait before relisting. That way your azz is covered.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero_24||11-28-2001||07:23 AM||||I realized after the auction that I should have listed a time to contact after the auction ended.  Email is everywhere, I made it a point when I was on vacation to go to a PC to email the winner of an auction.  I know everyone thinks the same way, but I guess you learn.  ||||reg||9
Z||000006||thomas_l||11-28-2001||09:14 AM||||Get on eBay and win that ass kicking someone posted a while ago and just send it to him  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000007||Ken Wittlief||11-28-2001||09:30 AM||||if soemone hoses you on ebay - unless you loose a lot of money - let it go and relist the item.<P> If you give someone negative feedback over a minor thing they might come back and trash your feedback - its not worth the grief. 95% of the time transactions will go smoothy - take the other 5% as the cost of doing business and forget about it. Its not worth getting PO'd over.||||reg||10
Z||000008||Rex||11-28-2001||05:43 PM||||I guess someones computer could go down.<BR>I think I'd just let it slide, and not do business with then again.I saw they had the shades on they may not know whats going on or what day it is.   LOL||||reg||1
